      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What are the property tax rates on a Boerne investment property?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "For a home inside Boerne city limits in Boerne ISD, the 2025 adopted rates per $100 of taxable value were Boerne ISD 1.0109, City of Boerne 0.4716 and Kendall County 0.377, plus any special district on the parcel such as a MUD, the WCID or the groundwater conservation district."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can I run a short-term rental in Boerne as an investment?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes, under City of Boerne Ordinance No. 2023-09, which requires a $200 two-year permit, a safety inspection inside city limits, $500,000 per-occurrence liability insurance and hotel occupancy tax of 13 percent combined. In residential zones an STR cannot operate within 200 feet of another STR on the same block face, which can disqualify a specific address."
