      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Occupancy is capped at two people per bedroom plus two additional people, so a three-bedroom sleeps eight. Events are prohibited, which removes event or venue income entirely. Hotel occupancy tax of 13 percent and a $500,000 per-occurrence liability insurance requirement are both real operating costs."
      }
    },
