      "name": "What county is Boerne, Texas in?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Boerne is the county seat of Kendall County. It is not in Bexar County and not in the City of San Antonio, so San Antonio ordinances do not apply. Property is appraised by Kendall Appraisal District, which is where homestead exemptions are filed and protests are heard."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Are Boerne ISD schools rated well?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Boerne ISD earned an A rating from the Texas Education Agency for six consecutive years, including the 2024 and 2025 rating years, scoring 92 points in the 2024-2025 ratings with 20 distinction designations. Not every campus rated A, so check the specific campus that serves a specific address."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Where does Boerne get its water?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "From three sources: Canyon Lake surface water purchased through the Guadalupe-Blanco River Authority, Boerne City Lake, and local wells in the Trinity Group aquifers. Groundwater in Kendall County is regulated by the Cow Creek Groundwater Conservation District, which sets drought stages. Check ccgcd.org for the current stage."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How far is Boerne from San Antonio?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "About 31 miles northwest of San Antonio via Interstate 10, roughly a 30 to 45 minute drive to downtown San Antonio depending on traffic. Boerne's practical orientation is toward San Antonio for medical care, the airport and major shopping."
